implementationPlan.description:
VERIFY ONCE, fresh (DoD 1 to 3). Gate in snapshots only: never run npm or node tests in the shared checkout (GLOBAL rail; mem:gotcha-vscode-gate-from-wsl). Use the checkRef's env -i PATH for every node and npm call.
1) Mutant sweep (mem:pattern-mutant-sweep-in-gate-snapshot; mem:gotcha-vscode-wire-parity-test-harness point 6). cp --parents chat.js and MoeDaemonClient.ts over step 1's snapshot (now 22/22 pass). Use a scratch node driver OUTSIDE the checkout: the prototype's /mnt/d/moe-scratch/vsc24-architect-prototype/mutants.cjs, re-anchored on your code. Keep it for QA. The driver:
- applies one exact-string replacement per mutant to the SNAPSHOT copy only, and asserts the anchor hits exactly once (a miss is an anchor fix, never a code change);
- runs `node --test tests/wire-parity.test.cjs`;
- counts a kill only on a non-zero exit WITH ERR_ASSERTION in the output;
- restores the file in finally.
The mutants:
- M1 no general preference (channels[0]);
- M2 the last general-type channel wins;
- M3 channelCreated without the id filter;
- M4 channelCreated replaces in place instead of filter plus push;
- M5 channelCreated without the auto-select;
- M6 the page id guard reduced to truthiness;
- M7 the auto-select ignores an existing selection;
- M8 the client cache without the id filter;
- M9 the client fires before the cache write;
- M10 the client id guard removed;
- M11 the client `?? []` removed;
- M12 the client also fires _onStateChanged.
Expected: 12/12 killed (prototype-verified). A survivor is a test gap: strengthen the test, then re-run. Report killed/total.
2) Run the checkRef verbatim from the repo root (a new snapshot). Confirm exit 0, lint 0, compile 0 and node:test fail 0, and report the test count. Baseline at 78642f85: 556 tests (552 pass, 4 skip). Expect 566.
Error handling for a red run:
- A failure in a test file this task did not touch, traced to a peer's wip checkpoint, follows mem:gotcha-snapshot-gate-peer-wip-checkpoint.
- A failure in A1 to C4 means the change broke VSC-6 behaviour: fix the code, never the VSC-6 test.
- If a run hangs, kill only the PID you started: no pkill, killall or pattern kill (GLOBAL rule).
Delete both snapshots afterwards, by their printed literal paths.
